// @run
// @log 5
// THE FLOOR THIS FILE PINNED IS LIFTED — the graduation its own header asked for ("flip it
// when the floor lifts"). The name is kept because `variant-annotated-global-floor.vl` and
// the CHANGELOG entry that introduced both name this file, and because the sibling floor
// made the identical graduation under its own name.
//
// WHAT IT PINNED. An UN-ANNOTATED module global whose object literal's field-name SET
// equals a union VARIANT's. `collectAnonShapes` skips such a literal
// (`objVariantName(ai) != ""`, on the reading that it will be boxed as an arm) and a
// variant's own `TypeDecl` is deliberately absent from the struct table (`collectS` skips
// `variantIndexOf(…) >= 0` — the variant table owns it). So the literal got no layout from
// either table and the read had no receiver: `field access but no struct type declared`.
//
// WHY IT LIFTS, AND IT IS NOT THE GUARD (silent-class-inventory D244). The load-bearing
// guard is untouched — deleting `&& objVariantName(ai) == ""` still reddens 7 of the `@run`
// corpus, `types/variant-as-value.vl` among them, and that measurement is why the repair
// was never a relaxation. What changed is the CELL, not the anon pass: `globalKind`'s
// `ObjLit` arm grew the rung `collectLocals` has carried since D51 — where the struct table
// has no row for the field set, the arm is the only nominal claimant, so the global is the
// kind-8 variant and the read resolves through the VARIANT field table, which is the same
// route the annotated spelling beside it takes. The literal never needs an `#anon` row.
//
// THE HEADER'S CONTROL TABLE WAS RE-RUN AGAINST `322c07f2` AND THREE ROWS OF IT WERE
// ALREADY STALE THERE — recorded rather than deleted, because a stale control reads as a
// live boundary: the LOCAL spelling, the `{k: 5}` no-variant-shares-the-fieldset spelling
// and the `Inner`/`Outer` deeper spelling all RUN on the merge base, so only the module-
// global cell this file holds was still floored. The two rows that still discriminate: the
// annotated binding `: Outer` is `variant-annotated-global-floor.vl` (already `@run`), and
// dropping the union lowers the literal as an ordinary anonymous struct.
type Outer = { p: i32 }
type U = Outer | i32

const g = { p: 5 }
print(g.p)
